msgctxt "916"
msgid "Just a minute, Kiryu-kun. IF7 isn't a two-player game, you know."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "928"
msgid ""
"You're gonna have to come back when you're alone. I'll be waiting right "
"here."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "940"
msgid "Hmm... Yes, you'll do."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "952"
msgid ""
"You're gonna have to come back when you're alone. I'll be waiting right "
"here."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "964"
msgid "I'm back."
msgstr "Sono tornata."

msgctxt "976"
msgid "Great Scott! You beat him!? So is Amon... dead?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "988"
msgid "No, he's still alive."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1000"
msgid "What!? Kiryu-san! You let him live? He'll just come after you again!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1012"
msgid "Maybe. But I don't plan to let him turn me into a murderer. Besides..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1024"
msgid "Besides?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1036"
msgid "If he does come back, I can just beat him again."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1048"
msgid ""
"You're an amazing man, Kazuma Kiryu. You really are some kind of... what did"
" he say? \"Experience beast.\""
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1060"
msgid "...Watch who you're calling a beast."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1072"
msgid "Oh, no, it wasn't me. That's what Amon called you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1084"
msgid "What did he mean by that?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1096"
msgid ""
"He said that your greatest strength is your ability to build off your "
"experiences to make yourself stronger at an almost preternatural rate."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1108"
msgid ""
"I supposed that made you a beast in Amon's eyes. After watching you fight in"
" IF7, I'm starting to understand what he was talking about."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1120"
msgid ""
"In any case, I'm glad everything worked out. I doubt Amon will be back any "
"time soon, and maybe now, my life can get back to normal, too."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1132"
msgid "What do you plan to do now?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1144"
msgid ""
"The president of a game company has been chasing me for some time trying to "
"get me to sign up with them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1156"
msgid ""
"I'm finally in a position where I can take him up on it. It's a small "
"company, but I'm ready for a fresh start."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1168"
msgid "I see."
msgstr "Capisco."

msgctxt "1180"
msgid ""
"But until then, I'll be here. At least for a little while longer. Stop by "
"anytime."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1192"
msgid ""
"I wouldn't mind watching one of your performances again, either. Hehehe."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1204"
msgid "All right. I just might do that."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1252"
msgid "Ah, Kiryu-kun. Good to see you. Have you come to play?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1264"
msgid "That's right."
msgstr "Esatto."

msgctxt "1276"
msgid "......"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1288"
msgid "What's going on?"
msgstr "Cosa succede?"

msgctxt "1300"
msgid "I'm sorry, Kiryu-san, but there's something I've been hiding from you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1312"
msgid "What's that?"
msgstr "Cos'è?"

msgctxt "1324"
msgid ""
"The truth is that I'm on the run. Not from a loan shark or anything, no, no,"
" no. The man pursuing me is much worse."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1336"
msgid "And... I knew about you before you ever came to try my invention."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1348"
msgid "How?"
msgstr "Come?"

msgctxt "1360"
msgid ""
"The man pursuing me. He told me about you. And he's the one who commissioned"
" the creation of this machine."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1372"
msgid "You're talking about Amon, aren't you?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1384"
msgid ""
"You knew? The whole time!? And you still played along? That's incredible..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1396"
msgid "What does Amon commissioning this machine have to do with me?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1408"
msgid ""
"This machine was created with a single purpose in mind: defeat Kazuma Kiryu."
" You!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1420"
msgid ""
"Amon visited my office approximately one year ago, requesting that I build a"
" special machine for him. He brought with him a number of attaché cases "
"filled with cash."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1432"
msgid ""
"I refused at first. Our newly released YF6 was a smash hit, and as a result,"
" I had more cash than I could possibly spend."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1444"
msgid "But then... he showed me his blueprints. They were astounding..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1456"
msgid "Blueprints for what?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1468"
msgid ""
"A truly incredible machine. It uses a person's experiences to enact battles "
"within their mind with authenticity that rivals reality itself! I could "
"scarely believe it!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1480"
msgid ""
"It was a dream come true: build a revolutionary machine and get paid to do "
"it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1492"
msgid ""
"I'm not one for mysticism, but Amon had what can only be described as a "
"forboding aura about him. The scars all over his body didn't help, either. "
"Naturally, I couldn't refuse."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1504"
msgid ""
"Still, I deliberated for three sleepless nights until I finally agreed. But "
"that Amon... he's an even more formidable man than I had ever imagined..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1516"
msgid "In what way?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1528"
msgid ""
"Amon played the first prototype I produced. I have never seen anyone fight "
"like that. It was incredible."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1540"
msgid ""
"As I watched Amon play, the game generated locations from all over the "
"world, and his myriad opponents were of all ages, races, and creeds. He "
"slaughtered each of them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1552"
msgid ""
"Think about what kind of life he must have led to meet and kill all those "
"people... It's chilling."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1564"
msgid "That's all the machine did? It's just a training tool, then, isn't it?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1576"
msgid ""
"I thought so at first, too. When he commissioned me, I assumed he just "
"wanted to use it to train himself."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1588"
msgid ""
"It wasn't until he gave me the plans for the additional feature that its "
"true purpose became clear."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1600"
msgid "What?"
msgstr "Cosa?"

msgctxt "1612"
msgid "It contains a kind of feedback system."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1624"
msgid "What's that?"
msgstr "Cos'è?"

msgctxt "1636"
msgid ""
"You've already experienced it. It analyzes the techniques of your opponents "
"and helps you integrate them into your own mind."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1648"
msgid ""
"Amon wanted to use it to learn the techniques of one particular opponent: "
"you!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1660"
msgid ""
"So those abilities I learned... They didn't just come to me through "
"inspiration...?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1672"
msgid "Not quite."
msgstr "Non proprio!"

msgctxt "1684"
msgid "What do you mean, \"not quite\"?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1696"
msgid ""
"According to the blueprints, the player should only be able to learn "
"techniques used by their opponents."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1708"
msgid ""
"But you have learned techniques seemingly independent of the opponents "
"you've faced. It's baffling."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1720"
msgid ""
"You have somehow pushed the machine beyond its programming. You defy "
"explanation, Kazuma Kiryu. The human race is full of wonders."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1732"
msgid "Why did you decide to run from Amon?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1744"
msgid ""
"One of the virtual opponents Amon had fought was a man he had hired to do a "
"job for him and who he murdered once the job was done. I realized he'd "
"eventually kill me, too."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1756"
msgid ""
"Besides, my passion is creating entertainment. The machine Amon commissioned"
" me to build was only going to bring more suffering into the world."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1768"
msgid ""
"I realized I had made a terrible mistake when I agreed to help him. He's a "
"monster in human skin."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1780"
msgid ""
"Among the opponents Amon had fought, two had given him trouble. One was an "
"old man. The other was you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1792"
msgid ""
"When I inquired as to who you were, he just grimaced and said, \"Kazuma "
"Kiryu.\" You were one of the only ones who could stand up to Amon."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1804"
msgid ""
"You were the one he built the machine to defeat. If I could somehow find "
"you..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1816"
msgid ""
"I knew from the simulations that Amon had fought you twice in Kamurocho."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1828"
msgid ""
"Kamurocho is packed with people. I thought I might be able to escape both "
"Amon and my creditors there, and I'd have a chance at meeting you, as well."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1840"
msgid ""
"I recognized you the moment I laid eyes on you. It was exhilarating meeting "
"you in the flesh. You're a legend, Kazuma Kiryu."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1852"
msgid "Don't you think that Amon knows about this place by now?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1864"
msgid ""
"No, I'm certain he doesn't know I'm here. He must not find out I'm in "
"Kamurocho."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1936"
msgid "Hehehe. The time has come at last!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1948"
msgid "Amon!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1960"
msgid "What!?"
msgstr "Cosa!?"

msgctxt "1972"
msgid "Your time has come, Kazuma Kiryu! Mwahahaha!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1984"
msgid "It's been a long time, Amon. What do you want with me?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1996"
msgid ""
"The Amon Clan does not look kindly on defeat. Defeat is death. Those who are"
" defeated forfeit their right to live."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2008"
msgid "But I have survived the unsurvivable. I have been cleansed by death."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2020"
msgid "And I am still alive, Kazuma Kiryu. I am still alive!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2032"
msgid ""
"The words \"hate\" and \"loathing\" do not begin to describe my contempt for"
" you..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2044"
msgid ""
"The first step to victory is to know thy enemy... And I know everything "
"about you. Your phone number. Your friends."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2056"
msgid ""
"The people you'd die to protect. And getting that information was a trivial "
"matter. Hehehe."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2068"
msgid "What!?"
msgstr "Cosa!?"

msgctxt "2080"
msgid "Thank you for your help in collecting data on Kiryu, Doctor Minamida."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2092"
msgid "But I did no such thing!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2104"
msgid "Ah, but you did."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2116"
msgid ""
"While you were snoring like a drunken sow, I extracted the machine's log "
"data."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2128"
msgid "I'm an assassin, Doctor. I know how to avoid waking the soon-dead."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2140"
msgid ""
"Hah! The log data? That won't do you any good without my invention. You "
"can't use the feedback system without it!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2152"
msgid "Don't be a fool, Minamida."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2164"
msgid ""
"Who gave you the plans for the machine in the first place? It's not your "
"invention; it's mine. And of course, I've already built one."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2176"
msgid "What!? Then why did you bother having me make one!?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2188"
msgid "Simple. It was a test."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2200"
msgid ""
"I had to see if the technology would work on ordinary people. But you "
"surprised me, Minamida."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2212"
msgid "Nrgh..."
msgstr "Ugh..."

msgctxt "2224"
msgid "And you're surprisingly skilled at hiding as well."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2236"
msgid "The day you left was the day I had planned to kill you off."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2248"
msgid "......"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2260"
msgid "Now listen to me, Kazuma Kiryu."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2272"
msgid "I hold your fate in my hands. Do you understand what that means?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2284"
msgid ""
"I have the information and the ability to make everyone you care about die "
"before your eyes."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2296"
msgid "Mwahahaha."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2308"
msgid "Amon! What do you want?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2320"
msgid ""
"It's simple. I want your life. But put any ideas of merely surrendering to "
"me out of your mind."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2332"
msgid ""
"I want to watch you struggle, Kazuma Kiryu. To fight tooth and nail up until"
" the very moment I crush you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2344"
msgid ""
"I know all of your skills as well as those of countless other hardened "
"killers. You could never hope to defeat me."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2356"
msgid "Mwahahaha."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2368"
msgid ""
"I will wait for you at the Mountainside Coliseum where we will not be "
"disturbed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2380"
msgid "I've sent a map to your cell phone."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2392"
msgid ""
"The area is completely deserted at night. Wait for nightfall, and then come."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2404"
msgid "Amon..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2416"
msgid ""
"I don't need you to answer, Kiryu. Listen well. If you fail to come, one "
"person you love will die every month."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2428"
msgid ""
"If you would rather live with that guilt, sadness, and fear, you're welcome "
"to."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2440"
msgid ""
"But know that once everyone you love is gone, I'll come after every person "
"who has ever known you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2452"
msgid ""
"I will snuff out the life of one person every month until your flame too "
"finally gutters out. Hehehe..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2512"
msgid ""
"I'm sorry for helping him, Kiryu-san. I had no idea what he was planning..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2524"
msgid "It's not your fault. This is who Amon is."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2536"
msgid ""
"But what are you going to do? How can you fight that monster? He knows "
"everything you do!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2548"
msgid "You heard what he said. I have no choice."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2560"
msgid "Well... I wish you godspeed, Kiryu-san."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2572"
msgid ""
"And remember, this isn't a game. If you lose, it's over. You'd better go "
"prepared... Not that I should have to tell you that."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2584"
msgid "I know."
msgstr "Lo so."

msgctxt "2596"
msgid "I'll wait for you, Kiryu-san. Bring me good news."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2608"
msgid "I will."
msgstr "Certo."

msgctxt "2620"
msgid ""
"(I'd better take a taxi to where Amon is... I can just show the driver the "
"map he sent me.)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2656"
msgid "Hey... Hey! Are you all right!?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2668"
msgid ""
"...\r\n"
"......\r\n"
"........."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2680"
msgid ""
"Good, good, you're coming around. I was worried I might've lost you... "
"Unfortunately, you appear to have lost your match."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2692"
msgid ""
"But don't let that discourage you. You're more than welcome to try as many "
"times as you like."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2752"
msgid "You won. Well done. I saw everything on the monitor."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2764"
msgid "Did you get anything out of the experience?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2776"
msgid ""
"Yeah... It felt like something was being burned into my brain. Like I got "
"some kind of inspiration from the moves my opponent was using."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2788"
msgid "You learned Asura Spirit!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2800"
msgid ""
"This is the final ability, gained by defeating your inner self.\r\n"
"Cancels Heat Mode in exchange for some health.\r\n"
"\r\n"
"Activation Method\r\n"
"Press <Action:Button_L3@Combat> and <Action:Button_R3@Combat> <Color:109,193,240,255>together in Heat Mode<Color:Default> <Color:255,255,150,255>if health is flashing<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2812"
msgid ""
"You appear to have learned a new fighting move. What a fascinating "
"phenomenon."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2824"
msgid ""
"There may be more techniques you can learn. Come back anytime and try again."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2848"
msgid "You got 2,000 EXP."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2908"
msgid "You won. Well done. I saw everything on the monitor."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2920"
msgid "Did you get anything out of the experience?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2932"
msgid "Not really."
msgstr "Non proprio."

msgctxt "2944"
msgid ""
"Well, that's not too unusual given the circumstances. Why don't you try "
"facing an opponent you've never beaten before?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2956"
msgid ""
"If you've beaten all the available opponents, you may have to experience new"
" fights in the real world before more become available in the game."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2968"
msgid ""
"But that's not to say you should throw yourself into danger for the sake of "
"a game, no, no, no! Here, take this for your trouble. Maybe it'll come in "
"handy."
msgstr ""

